{"packet_id":"D069-01","doc_id":"D069","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"algorithmic_rent_setting","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"FAIR Act algorithmic rent-setting ban","requirement":"Landlords may not subscribe to or use a coordinator's algorithmic services, coordinators may not facilitate pricing coordination or perform a coordinating function, and persons may not engage in parallel pricing coordination for residential dwelling units.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Applies to rental property owners, agents, representatives, subcontractors, coordinators, and any person performing a coordinating function for residential dwelling units in New Jersey.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":1,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Government entities using affordability controls excluded"},"exemptions":"Excludes spreadsheets without AI requiring human analysis; query-only databases; research/statistical use; free public rent estimates; equal-access brokerage databases that do not set rents; government entities using affordability controls.","penalty":"Violations are violations of the New Jersey Antitrust Act, whose enforcement and penalty provisions (C.56:9-6 through 9-17) apply.","effective_date":"2027-07-01","citation":"P.L. 2026, c. 43, § 4","quoted_span":"It shall be unlawful and a violation of the “New Jersey Antitrust Act,” P.L.1970, c.73 (C.56:9-1 et seq.) for:
a.     a rental property owner, or any agent,
representative, or subcontractor thereof, to receive, subscribe to, contract
for, or otherwise exchange any form of consideration in return for the use of,
the services of a coordinator;","interaction":"Municipalities may not enact conflicting ordinances; act supplements New Jersey Antitrust Act and does not limit its sections 6 through 17.","confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
